# First Year Student Essays in Humanities and Social Sciences: The Need for New Paradigms.

**Authors:** Lukeman, Howard

## Abstract
Analysis of essays by first-year college students on humanities and social science subjects suggests that problems in style and structure stem from student misunderstandings of discipline-specific assumptions and conventions concerning critical analysis and &quot;argument.&quot; Discussions and models can help students create new, academically acceptable paradigms of analytical thinking and writing. (SV)

